# Force line-ending normalization to never touch binary files, regardless
# of what Git's own binary-detection heuristic guesses. Without this, a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true can attempt LF/CRLF conversion
# on files like PDFs — which corrupts them, since the conversion has no
# concept of a compressed binary stream.

* text=auto

*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary

# Reviewer responses are evidence: they are committed exactly as the provider's
# stream delivered them. `* text=auto` above would normalise their line endings
# at commit and rewrite them again at checkout, so a file that is supposed to be
# a verbatim record would no longer be byte-identical to what arrived. -text
# switches normalisation off for that directory only.
docs/audit_reports/** -text
